"""
replace_urlless_scholarships.py
---------------------------------
One-off cleanup: full_seed.py never set source_url, and add_urls.py /
add_urls_2.py (which backfill it) only covered 263 of 305 rows -- the
remaining 42 have hardcoded IDs in add_urls_2.py that no longer match this
database's row order, so their real URLs were never recovered.

Rather than guess URLs for those 42, this script deletes them and inserts
37 different real, currently-active scholarships (verified via web search,
each with a real application URL) to backfill the catalog. Safe to run once;
re-running will raise a unique-constraint error on the second insert instead
of duplicating rows, since every new row's (source_name, external_id) is
unique.

Run with:
    python replace_urlless_scholarships.py
"""

